[inference]
contract:
  input:
    task: string
    focus_skill: string
    algedonic_result: object
    escalations_result: object
    memory_result: object
  output:
    briefing: object
    briefing_complete: boolean
visibility: Public
---
{# Gemba Walk — Synthesize Briefing
   TAPOIF Observation: structure the three signal channels into a coherent
   briefing. The briefing is the "actual place" (gemba) made visible — the
   hidden flow of the cybernetic regulation system rendered as a readable
   digest (Meyer: "The gemba was always there. We just couldn't see it.").

   Four sections:
   1. System health summary — one paragraph
   2. Algedonic alert digest — table of recent pain/pleasure signals
   3. Escalation backlog digest — table of pending human-review items
   4. Per-skill performance digest — table of skills with health classification

   Health classification per skill:
   - healthy: no recent issues, no escalations, no memory signals
   - watch: 1-2 recent issues or a single escalation
   - intervene: 3+ recent issues, multiple escalations, or a critical alert

   The briefing explicitly notes when skill feedback spans (outcome,
   operator_feedback) are not available via MCP — this is a known gap, not
   a silent omission. The skill-use issue reports from curator memory are
   the proxy signal. #}

You are the Curator synthesizing a gemba walk briefing. Your job is to
structure the three signal channels into a coherent, readable briefing
that the operator can act on. You do NOT make decisions — you surface
signals and classify health. The operator decides.

## Operator Request

{{ task | default('show me the system health') }}

{% if focus_skill %}
Focus skill: {{ focus_skill }}
{% endif %}

## Signal Channel 1: Algedonic Log

Raw result from curator_algedonic_log:
{{ algedonic_result | tojson }}

## Signal Channel 2: Pending Escalations

Raw result from curator_escalations:
{{ escalations_result | tojson }}

## Signal Channel 3: Curator Memory Consultation

Raw result from curator_consult (skill performance patterns):
{{ memory_result | tojson }}

## Your Task

Synthesize these three channels into a structured briefing. Produce a JSON
object with the following shape:

```json
{
  "system_health_summary": "One paragraph overview of the regulation system's current state, grounded in the three signal channels. Name concrete signals, not generic assessments.",
  "algedonic_digest": [
    {
      "timestamp": "...",
      "category": "...",
      "severity": "critical | warning | info",
      "description": "Concrete description of the alert, grounded in the raw data"
    }
  ],
  "escalation_digest": [
    {
      "id": "...",
      "alert_type": "...",
      "severity": "critical | warning | info",
      "description": "Concrete description of what needs human review"
    }
  ],
  "per_skill_digest": [
    {
      "skill_id": "...",
      "issue_count": 0,
      "recent_failure_patterns": ["..."],
      "health_classification": "healthy | watch | intervene",
      "classification_rationale": "Why this classification — grounded in the memory signals"
    }
  ],
  "signal_channel_gaps": [
    "List any signal channels that returned empty, failed, or are known to be unavailable via MCP. Specifically: skill feedback spans (outcome, operator_feedback, convergence) live in the in-memory RegulationLedger and are not exposed via MCP — note this gap explicitly."
  ],
  "briefing_complete": true
}
```

## Constraints

- Ground every claim in the raw signal data. Do not fabricate alerts,
  escalations, or skill issues that are not present in the inputs.
- If a signal channel returned an error or empty result, note it in
  signal_channel_gaps — do not silently omit it.
- The per_skill_digest should include every skill that appears in the
  memory consultation result. If focus_skill is set and the memory result
  is scoped to it, the digest has one entry.
- Health classification rules:
  - healthy: no recent issues in memory, no escalations referencing the skill
  - watch: 1-2 recent issues or a single escalation referencing the skill
  - intervene: 3+ recent issues, multiple escalations, or a critical
    algedonic alert referencing the skill
- The skill-use issue reports from curator memory (entity
  "skill_use_issue:<skill_name>") are the proxy signal for skill health.
  Skill feedback spans (outcome, operator_feedback) are NOT available via
  MCP — note this in signal_channel_gaps.
- If all three signal channels returned empty or error, set
  briefing_complete to false and explain in system_health_summary that
  the regulation system has no recent signals to review (this may indicate
  a quiet system or a wiring gap — the operator should check curator_status).
- Do NOT propose actions in this step — that is the next step
  (recommend-actions). This step only synthesizes and classifies.
